My 2 zorkmids worth:

I started with The Colour of Magic, and have read them mostly in
order, except for a few in the middle which were slow to show up in
the US (except for the $12 imported versions).  Pratchett has
definitely gotten better with age.  Many of his later books are MUCH
better than the early books.  I liked reading the first few in order,
as you are introduced to main characters.  For instance (and possibly
from a faulty memory), Mort introduces Mort (duh), DEATH, and possibly
Susan.  Susan plays a key role in several of the later books
(especially the recent Thief of Time, which IMO is one of the better
ones).  For stories and because I love the witches, Witches Abroad and
Wyrd Sisters are great, the former being a play on the Cinderella
story.  In fact, the main character is a poor stepsister called...
wait for it... Ember Ella.  Tee hee...

In fact, some of my favorite books are the ones in which a well known
story/fairy tale is recast in Discworld (Witches Abroad and Maskerade
come immediately to mind).

